            <ArticleTitle>Caring for a patient with malodorous leg ulcers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50, 52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with leg ulceration who experience symptoms of pain and malodour can become isolated and suffer psychological problems. Peter Cooke describes a patient who experienced these problems and identifies the importance of patient involvement in planning care.</AbstractText>
